.TH CDCSTORE-LIST 1 "October 2026" "cdcstore" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cdcstore\-list \- list a cdcstore repository, or print its chunk files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cdcstore\-list
[\-l] [\-s] [\-k] REPO [PATTERN...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Without options, prints one stored path per line (folders end in /). With PATTERNs only the matching entries are listed. A PATTERN is a path (a file, or a folder with its contents) or a quoted wildcard; none means everything.
.PP
With \-k it prints the files to hand to a sorter and an archiver: the path of cdcstore.idx first (it belongs in the archive too), then the chunk files, one per line, in chunk\-number order, which is the order the data was added. The sortof tools keep cdcstore.idx first without sorting or reading it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-l
Long listing: type, mode, size, date and path.
.TP
.B \-s
Print the repository's numbers instead: files, sizes, unique chunks, and the same for the selection.
.TP
.B \-k
Print cdcstore.idx and then the chunk files. With PATTERNs, only the chunks those files use are printed, each once, in the order they are first used.
.TP
.B \-h
Print help.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.RS
cdcstore\-list \-l REPO 'games/*'
cdcstore\-list \-k REPO | sortof\-cdcsort \- > list.txt
.RE
.fi
.sp
